<description>
Fill each vertical foreground band's background cells with the color of the next band to its right.

Input structure
- The dominant color is the background.
- Each other color occupies a separate vertical band defined by that color's
  minimum and maximum columns.
- Within a band, all cells are either that band's color or background.

Rule
- Order the bands from left to right.
- In each band, replace background pixels with the color of the next band in
  that order, wrapping from the rightmost band back to the leftmost.
- Preserve all existing foreground pixels and all background pixels outside
  the bands.

Key insight
- The column bands form a cyclic palette legend: a band's gaps are completed
  by borrowing the color from its right-hand neighbor, not by changing the
  band's existing pixels.
</description>
<annotation>
{
  "type": "move_in_order",
  "src": "foreground band colors s, one per vertical non-bg column span, ordered left-to-right",
  "dst": "background gap masks d inside the same vertical band spans, ordered left-to-right",
  "match_cond": "d_i receives color s_{i+1}; the rightmost d receives s_0",
  "transform": "paint only the matched background gaps; preserve existing foreground pixels and background separator columns"
}
</annotation>
<generation_spec>
```yaml
spec:
  grid: 10 rows x 8 cols [observed]
  colors: 4 distinct -- 1 background (most frequent) + 3 foreground
  layout: |
    Grid = Band_0 | Sep | Band_1 | Sep | ... | Band_{n-1}
    Bands span full width (leftmost starts col 0, rightmost ends at last col)
    Separators are exactly 1 column wide, filled entirely with bg
  bands:
    count: 3 [observed], solver requires >=2
    width: 1-3 cols each; total band cols = grid_cols - (count-1)
    content: each cell is either the band's fg color or bg
    density: 0.30-0.75 of cells are fg (must have both fg and bg cells)
    pattern: irregular/freeform pixel placement within band
  transformation:
    rule: for each band i, replace bg cells with color of band (i+1) % n
    preserve: all existing fg pixels and all bg outside bands unchanged

generation_strategy:
  approach: direct input construction (simple enough structure)
  steps:
    1. Pick grid dimensions (rows=8-12, cols=7-10)
    2. Choose 4 distinct colors; assign one as bg
    3. Choose number of bands (2-4) and allocate column widths (1-3 each) such that total_band_cols + (num_bands-1) separators = grid_cols
    4. Assign one fg color per band; order bands left-to-right with 1-col bg separators between them
